<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
	<application android:allowBackup="true" android:icon="@mipmap/appicon" android:roundIcon="@mipmap/appicon_round" android:supportsRtl="true"></application>
	<!--
		No permissions are declared. The app reads a bundled corpus, stores notes and progress in a
		local SQLite database, and never opens a socket: INTERNET and ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE came from
		the MAUI template and were never used. Tapping a study link hands a URL to Launcher, which
		is the browser's or Gospel Library's network access, not ours.

		Debug builds still get INTERNET injected by the Android SDK for the debugger; the shipped
		Release manifest has none. Verify with the merged manifest under obj/ before assuming.

		Before adding one back, check it is genuinely exercised - an unused permission is a Play
		policy hygiene finding and forces Data Safety answers we would otherwise not have to make.
	-->
</manifest>